## Summary

| Severity | Count | Pattern |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 Critical | 6 | Method called, zero assertions — **cannot detect any bug** |
| 🟠 High | 4 | `IsNotNull` on types that are never null — **assertion is tautological** |
| 🟡 Medium | 5+ | Missing edge/error cases — **no coverage of failure paths** |

**Root cause:** Every test follows the same anti-pattern — call the method, maybe assert `IsNotNull`, call it done. This is the "coverage theater" pattern: the coverage tool sees every line executed, but no test actually verifies a behavioral contract. A regression in any method (wrong price, wrong SKU, swapped fields) would pass the entire suite.
